{"title":"With hopes of victory fading, Ukraine's fight against Russia could get even harder in 2024 (Cnbc | World Business News Leader, 2023-12-25T23:36:00+00:00)","text":"With hopes of victory fading, Ukraine's fight against Russia could get even harder in 2024 (Cnbc | World Business News Leader, 2023-12-25T23:36:00+00:00)
Aid and politics

Another year of war in Europe has undoubtedly drained Western military resources and the political appetite to maintain massive amounts of military aid for Ukraine. Ongoing funding for Ukraine is far from secure in 2024 given the fact that the U.S. presidential election could herald a seismic change in the attitude toward and support for Kyiv. Specifically, all eyes are on former U.S. President Donald Trump, the Republican front-runner, who cultivated close relations with his Russian counterpart Vladimir Putin during his presidency. There are concerns that, given Trump's previous good relations with Moscow and "America First" policy, aid for Ukraine could be shelved rapidly. Defense analysts agree that much of the outlook for Ukraine is dependent on the outcome of the U.S. vote. "I think it's important to understand the extent to which Ukraine is reliant on the U.S. right now, because it's quite significantly more reliant on the U.S.","entities":["Russia","military aid","Ukraine","Vladimir Putin","Europe","CNBC","Kyiv","U.S. presidential election","With hopes of victory fading, Ukraine's fight against Russia could get even harder in 2024","war in Europe","Moscow","America First policy","Defense analysts","U.S.","Donald Trump"],"facts":["People are turning to Snap Map for firsthand perspectives from Gaza -MENTIONS-> Russia","'Too big to fail' Egypt faces economic crisis but has an anti-Gaza refugee policy. Israel and the U.S. hope that will change -MENTIONS-> Russia","Hitting the Books: We are the frogs in the boiling pot, it's time we started governing like it. -MENTIONS-> Russia","Deepfake election risks trigger EU call for more generative AI safeguards -MENTIONS-> Russia","Dissecting impact of Israel-Hamas conflict on markets -MENTIONS-> Russia"]}

{"title":"With hopes of victory fading, Ukraine's fight against Russia could get even harder in 2024 (Cnbc | World Business News Leader, 2023-12-25T23:36:00+00:00)","text":"With hopes of victory fading, Ukraine's fight against Russia could get even harder in 2024 (Cnbc | World Business News Leader, 2023-12-25T23:36:00+00:00)
With both Ukraine and Russia investing heavily in the war, it's unlikely there will be any negotiations to end the conflict or agree to a cease-fire. Defense analysts argue that neither side would want to go into negotiations unless they're in a position of strength and able to dictate terms. "In the case of a Republican winning the presidential election next year, especially if that's Donald Trump, who seems to be the front-runner, and [if] funding is decreased substantially, then there will be increased pressure on Ukraine to negotiate," Mario Bikarski, a Europe and Russia analyst at the Economist Intelligence Unit, told CNBC.

A Ukrainian tank drives along the field on December 7, 2023 in Avdiivka, Ukraine. Kostya Liberov | Getty Images","entities":["Getty Images","CNBC","With hopes of victory fading, Ukraine's fight against Russia could get even harder in 2024","Avdiivka","Ukraine","Russia","war","Mario Bikarski","Economist Intelligence Unit","Kostya Liberov","presidential election","Donald Trump"],"facts":["Which M.L.B. Playoff Team Has the Most Daunting Home Field? We Ranked Them. -MENTIONS-> Getty Images","Video games in 2023: Acquisitions, layoffs, unions -MENTIONS-> Getty Images","From Justin Timberlake to Sam Asghari: A timeline of Britney Spears’ relationships -MENTIONS-> Getty Images","West Indies v England: fifth and deciding men’s T20 cricket international – live -MENTIONS-> Getty Images","Amazon sellers sound off on the FTC's 'long-overdue' antitrust case -MENTIONS-> Getty Images"]}

